      "page": 3,
      "text": "1. Implementation\n\nThe document has been created and approved by the General Assembly of 29.11.2025.\nThe document and its rules will be implemented from the 2029 season (01/01/2029).\nCompetitors will have 3 seasons to align their equipment with this document and its rules.\n\n2. Definition\n\nBarbutes are a design of helmet growing extremely popular during the 15th century. They see an\nextensive use and evolution between approximately 1430 to 1500.\n\nBarbutes tend to be locally used in Italy.\nBarbutes are worn alone or with an addition of a gorget of plate or mail.\n\nBarbutes can be of different designs: T shape or Y shape. The term “shape” refers to the opening for the\neyes and mouth.\n\nBarbutes type helmets are Approved for 15th century armors of matching design.\n\nBarbutes type helmets are Denied for 14th century and Transitional armors.\n\nT-shaped Barbute\n\nSJ » i\nJ\n\nBcrbutes v. 26.1 3/11",
