      "text": "4. Requirements\n\n4.1. General Requirements\n\nReproductions must closely resemble the appearance and proportions of historical sources.\n\nA particular attention must be paid to the crest on top of the Barbute, often forgotten by modern\narmorers.\n\nyw\n\nAny metal part of the helmet must conform to the “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations\ndocument.\n\nAny textile or leather part of the helmet must conform to the “Textiles and Leather” document.\n\n4.2. Visor\n\nVisors must not be too long or too short, it must respect the proportions of historical sources.\n\nIt is allowed to add a metal plate to protect the throat. Such a plate must be strong enough to endure full\ncontact fight and must be concealed under the aventail.\n\n4.3. Eyes and Mouth slot\n\nEyes and Mouth slots must resemble sources for the visor (T shape or Y shape).\nEyes and Mouth slots should not exceed 25 mm tall to prevent any injury, as a safety recommendation.\nIt is Allowed to add:\n\n● Up to five (5) safety Eye bars: one (1) in the middle and two (2) on each side of the Eye slots,\n● Up to five (5) safety Eye bars on the mouth slot,\nIt is allowed to use a T shaped-Eye bar at the junction of the Eye slots and the Mouth slot.\n\nIt is allowed to use slanted safety Eye bars for barbute with Y shape only.\nEye bars must be welded internally or riveted internally.\nEye bars must conform to the “Eye bars” document.\n\n4.4. Gorget\n\nBarbutes are not designed to be worn with an aventail, unlike bascinets. Barbutes are worn with a\ngorget.\n\nBarbutes must be worn with a plate gorget, or a safe construction simulating a mail gorget as best as\npossible.\n\nGorget must be constructed in such a way as to protect its wearer. Mail gorget must integrate a grill of\nprotection or additional plates.\n\nChainmail gorget must conform to Chainmail Aventails requirements listed in the “Aventails” document.\nAdditional neck protection can be worn according to historical sources.\nAdditional neck protection not based on historical sources can be worn if concealed.\n\nBcrbutes v. 26.1 7/1",
